WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.601
Every morning was eventful at the March home, today being no different.

2
00:00:05.602 --> 00:00:09.024
Amy had overslept and was very cranky.

3
00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:13.845
Her hair, her most precious asset, looked limp and lifeless.

4
00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.991
"May I please be excused from school?

5
00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:26.762
I’m just not happy today," she whined, munching on a piece of dry bread that would have been warm and soft if she had gotten up in time to eat it.

6
00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:29.538
"Well, then we should all stay home.

7
00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:34.777
I’m not happy and neither is Meg," Jo shouted sarcastically from the foyer.

8
00:00:34.778 --> 00:00:39.231
Late as usual, the two older girls were hastening to get out the door,

9
00:00:39.232 --> 00:00:44.867
but Jo couldn’t find The Pirate’s Enigma , a book she had borrowed from Aunt

10
00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:50.680
March. "Where could that stupid book be?" Jo yelled in

11
00:00:50.681 --> 00:00:54.077
frustration. "Jo! Mind your tongue and mind your

12
00:00:54.078 --> 00:00:57.814
temper!" Mother rebuked as she yanked at Amy’s

13
00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:02.200
knots. "I’ll look for the book," Beth offered in her timid

14
00:01:02.201 --> 00:01:07.616
manner. "Pray for me that Aunt March won’t have an urge to hear that story read to her

15
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:18.444
today. I’ll just pretend to be deaf or have a sore throat if she does," Jo remarked, shoving her arms into her thick coat, and finally stepping outside the

16
00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:23.383
door. Blowing kisses at everyone, Meg and Jo began their trek to

17
00:01:23.384 --> 00:01:26.598
work. When Mother went to the window to wave at her

18
00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:33.570
girls, Amy reluctantly gathered her school books, got her lunch pail from Hannah, and dragged her feet to the

19
00:01:33.571 --> 00:01:39.566
foyer. "You’re so lucky you can stay home all day," Amy said wistfully to

20
00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:43.764
Beth. At other times when Amy said this Beth would shake her head and

21
00:01:43.765 --> 00:01:48.286
say, "You’re the lucky one. I wish I could go to

22
00:01:48.287 --> 00:01:55.830
school." Today, however, Beth did not say anything because inside she was feeling very

23
00:01:55.831 --> 00:02:00.477
lucky. Today she had something very special to look forward

24
00:02:00.478 --> 00:02:08.932
to. It seemed to take an eternity before everyone was finally gone. Beth was all by

25
00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:18.293
herself. The kitchen door of the March home faced the Laurence mansion, in particular the conservatory, where the object of Beth’s desire

26
00:02:18.294 --> 00:02:24.633
was. Beth, however, had a major obstacle to overcome first: her

27
00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:31.139
fear. "What if Mr. Laurence suddenly walks into the conservatory?" she said to

28
00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.447
herself. "What if Laurie hears me play and thinks I’m

29
00:02:35.448 --> 00:02:43.939
horrible. Then what if he tells Jo? What if the door locks after I’m inside and I can’t get

30
00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:52.349
out?" But no matter how many "what ifs" Beth could think of, her fear did not hold her back from the beautiful instrument

31
00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:56.048
inside. Taking a deep breath, she opened the kitchen

32
00:02:56.049 --> 00:03:03.047
door. Sticking her head out and checking to make sure no one was around, she took one brave step

33
00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:10.298
forward. Then, like a frightened field mouse, she scurried across the yard onto the stone pathway that led to the

34
00:03:10.299 --> 00:03:17.501
mansion. Pausing to cool her flushed cheeks, Beth felt like an intruder, as if she were entering a home not her

35
00:03:17.502 --> 00:03:26.699
own. Mr. Laurence, of course, had given his permission; yet, it was an odd sensation as Beth pushed open the glass doors to the

36
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:37.735
conservatory. As Mr. Laurence had promised, the room was empty, and as before Beth caught her breath when her gaze fell upon the beautiful

37
00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:45.574
piano. "Hello. I’m Beth." The magnificence of the musical instrument impelled her to introduce

38
00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:53.235
herself. Giggling, she continued, "Mr. Laurence says I must come every day and look after

39
00:03:53.236 --> 00:04:01.453
you." She lightly stroked the keys. "He doesn’t want you to get dusty or for your keys to get

40
00:04:01.454 --> 00:04:08.970
stuck." Even with Beth’s amateur touch, she knew none of the polished keys ever got

41
00:04:08.971 --> 00:04:15.408
stuck. "But just between you and me," she leaned closer to the piano, as if she were whispering a secret,

42
00:04:15.409 --> 00:04:20.034
"I was hoping he would ask so I could come and play music on you."

43
00:04:20.035 --> 00:04:25.784
Pulling the stool out, Beth carefully sat down on the soft velvet cushion.

44
00:04:25.785 --> 00:04:32.384
"Oh, look!" Beth reached out to open an old leather book resting on the stand.

45
00:04:32.385 --> 00:04:38.173
Inside was a collection of sheet music, many of them songs that Beth knew.

46
00:04:38.174 --> 00:04:43.565
"You even prepared music for me to play. How kind you are!"

47
00:04:43.566 --> 00:04:48.463
Beth lovingly patted the top of the piano.

48
00:04:48.464 --> 00:04:56.792
After taking a moment to select a song, Beth clenched and unclenched her fists, as she’d seen pianists do.

49
00:04:56.793 --> 00:05:00.923
Then, ever so cautiously, she began to play.

50
00:05:00.924 --> 00:05:07.464
At first, the sounds were timid, like Beth, and unsure, lacking confidence and power.

51
00:05:07.465 --> 00:05:15.978
However, as she practiced and became more acquainted with her new friend, she felt comfortable enough to open her soul.

52
00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:22.243
Oblivious to the passing of time, Beth fell into a world of sound and harmony.

53
00:05:22.244 --> 00:05:27.145
True to her word, Beth visited the conservatory every day.

54
00:05:27.146 --> 00:05:34.068
Even though Hannah scolded her for not eating properly or practicing so long that her bones were stiff and numb,

55
00:05:34.069 --> 00:05:39.756
Beth felt that nothing could give her greater happiness than the time she spent playing music.

56
00:05:39.757 --> 00:05:48.473
Unknown to Beth, she already had a couple of secret admirers who also were finding joy and comfort in her melodies.

57
00:05:48.474 --> 00:05:57.063
One of them should have been paying closer attention to his lessons, but found himself straining his ears to hear Beth’s music.

58
00:05:57.064 --> 00:06:01.168
After Laurie discovered he could hear Beth playing downstairs,

59
00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:06.596
he deliberately opened a window in the library in order to hear the music more clearly.

60
00:06:06.597 --> 00:06:13.555
"Must you keep that window open? It’s freezing in here," Mr. Brookes complained to his young pupil.

61
00:06:13.556 --> 00:06:19.051
Mr. Brookes was not amused since the temperature outside was way below zero.

62
00:06:19.052 --> 00:06:24.300
The other admirer chose to sit in his study, lean back in his chair,

63
00:06:24.301 --> 00:06:32.360
and remember the time when his own little girl’s music could be heard through those very walls.

64
00:06:32.361 --> 00:06:38.990
Since everyone was home on the weekends, Beth could not practice her beloved piano in the conservatory,

65
00:06:38.991 --> 00:06:43.882
but she continued to play the music in her mind wherever she was.

66
00:06:43.883 --> 00:06:47.565
One Saturday, after returning from the grocer’s with Hannah,

67
00:06:47.566 --> 00:06:53.488
Beth found herself encircled by her sisters, all of them shouting with excitement at once.

68
00:06:53.489 --> 00:06:57.067
"You’ve got a gift, Beth!" screamed Amy.

69
00:06:57.068 --> 00:07:00.573
"A gift?" Beth asked, confused.

70
00:07:00.574 --> 00:07:06.919
"Come see it. Come!" Jo took Beth’s arm and led her to the living room.

71
00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:14.337
As she stepped into the familiar room, Beth’s eyes immediately went to the corner where something new stood.

72
00:07:14.338 --> 00:07:18.426
It was a beautiful solid oak piano.

73
00:07:18.427 --> 00:07:24.687
"Is this really for me?" she whispered, her voice trembling.

74
00:07:24.688 --> 00:07:29.839
"Look at this card, Beth!" Jo swung a white envelope in her face.

75
00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.392
"Read it! Hurry, Beth!" Amy pleaded.

76
00:07:33.393 --> 00:07:40.216
"I can’t. I’m too nervous. Jo, can you read it for me, please?" asked Beth.

77
00:07:40.217 --> 00:07:45.175
Jo ripped the envelope open and read in a loud voice.

78
00:07:45.176 --> 00:07:51.983
My dearest Beth, I’m afraid you may not like what I am about to say.

79
00:07:51.984 --> 00:07:57.601
But I must confess that I have been listening to your beautiful music from my study.

80
00:07:57.602 --> 00:08:04.399
You may not realize it but your lovely melodies have brought much happiness back into my home.

81
00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:13.688
Therefore, as a token of my deepest appreciation, please accept this gift, which, at one time, belonged to my own daughter.

82
00:08:13.689 --> 00:08:19.179
May it bring much music and joy to your home and hearts, as it has done to mine.

83
00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:25.841
Your greatest admirer, Mr. Laurence

